.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt TTYS 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ttys
.Nd terminal initialization information
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/ttys
lists the terminals on which
.Xr init 8
runs login sessions.
Each line describes one terminal with these fields, separated by blanks:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar name
The terminal's device name, relative to
.Pa /dev .
.It Ar getty
The command
.Xr init 8
runs on the terminal, normally
.Dq Pa /usr/libexec/getty Ar type ;
the terminal's name is added as its last argument.
It must be quoted if it contains blanks.
.Cm none
runs nothing.
.It Ar type
The terminal type, set as
.Ev TERM
for the session.
.It Ar status
.Cm on
to run the command,
.Cm off
not to,
.Cm onifexists
to run it only if the device exists, or
.Cm onifconsole
only if the terminal is the system console.
.El
.Pp
Any further words are flags:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm secure
The superuser may log in on this terminal, and single-user mode does not ask
for root's password.
.It Cm insecure
The opposite of
.Cm secure ,
and the default.
.It Cm window Ns = Ns Ar command
A command to run before
.Ar getty .
.It Cm group Ns = Ns Ar name
Put the terminal in a group, for use by other programs.
.El
.Pp
A
.Ql #
begins a comment, which runs to the end of the line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/ttys -compact
.It Pa /etc/ttys
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
console	none			unknown	off	insecure
ttyv0	"/usr/libexec/getty Pc"	linux	on	insecure
ttyu1	"/usr/libexec/getty 3wire"	vt100	onifexists	insecure
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr emergency 8 ,
.Xr getty 8 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
file appeared in
.At v6 .
